    <bpmn:process id="W_W1176" name="W1176. Green Procurement &amp; Sustainable Vendor Certification Program" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Annual vendor sustainability assessment cycle; or new vendor onboarding per W36; or ESG reporting requirement per W694
Frequency: Annual assessment for top-100 vendors by spend; assessment integrated into new vendor onboarding; quarterly progress monitoring
Volume: ~100 vendors assessed annually (representing ~80% of COGS); assessment integrated into new vendor onboarding (~50–80/year)
Owner: Sustainability Lead
Participants: Category Manager, Procurement, Vendor, ESG Manager, VP Merchandising, External Sustainability Auditor
Source: workflow W1176 — Green Procurement &amp; Sustainable Vendor Certification Program</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1176_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1176_Lane1" name="Sustainability Lead">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1176_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1176_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1176_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1176_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1176_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1176_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1176_Lane2" name="Vendor">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1176_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1176_Lane3" name="Procurement">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1176_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1176_End13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1176_Start5" name="Annual vendor sustainability assessment cycle; or new vendor onboarding per W36; or ESG…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1176_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1176_Task6" name="Sustainability criteria definition">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Sustainability criteria definition: Sustainability Lead defines assessment criteria across 4 dimensions: (a) Environmental: carbon footprint disclosure, energy efficiency practices, waste management, water stewardship, packaging sustainability per W1175, hazardous substance compliance per W236; (b) Social: fair labor practices, living wage compliance, workplace safety, no child labor or forced labor (per W160 social compliance audit), diversity and inclusion; (c) Governance: anti-corruption policies per W656, ethical business practices, data privacy compliance, regulatory compliance history; (d) Supply chain transparency: sub-tier supplier visibility, conflict mineral sourcing, responsible sourcing of raw materials (timber, minerals, chemicals)
Responsible (R): Sustainability Lead
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 1 week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1176_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1176_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1176_Task7" name="Vendor self-assessment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Vendor self-assessment: Distribute annual sustainability self-assessment questionnaire to top-100 vendors via vendor portal per W705: (a) structured questionnaire with 40–50 questions across 4 dimensions; (b) evidence requirements: certifications (ISO 14001, ISO 45001, SA8000), environmental permits, labor compliance records; (c) vendors self-rate on 1–5 scale per criterion with supporting evidence; (d) submission deadline: 30 days
Responsible (R): Vendor / Procurement
Accountable (A): Sustainability Lead
Duration: 4 hours/vendor</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1176_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1176_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1176_Task8" name="Assessment &amp; scoring">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Assessment &amp; scoring: Sustainability Lead evaluates vendor submissions: (a) review self-assessment against evidence; (b) score each dimension on 1–5 scale; (c) calculate overall sustainability score; (d) classify vendors: Green (≥ 4.0 overall): certified sustainable, preferred vendor status; Yellow (3.0–3.9): meets minimum standards, improvement plan recommended; Orange (2.0–2.9): below standard, corrective action plan required within 6 months; Red (&lt; 2.0): fails minimum standards, vendor relationship review — potential termination
Responsible (R): Sustainability Lead
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 2 hours/vendor</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1176_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1176_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1176_Task9" name="On-site verification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: On-site verification: For Green-rated vendors seeking certification and Orange/Red-rated vendors: (a) Sustainability Lead or External Auditor conducts on-site verification visit at vendor facility; (b) verify self-assessment claims against actual practices; (c) inspect: waste management facilities, worker conditions, safety equipment, chemical storage; (d) for import vendors: engage third-party audit firm per W160 for factory audit; (e) verification report with findings and scoring adjustment
Responsible (R): Sustainability Lead / External Auditor
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 1–2 days/vendor</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1176_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1176_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1176_Task10" name="Corrective action &amp; improvement">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Corrective action &amp; improvement: For Yellow/Orange vendors: (a) issue corrective action plan with specific improvement targets and 6-month timeline; (b) provide resources: best practice guides, referral to sustainability consultants; (c) quarterly check-in on progress; (d) re-assessment after 6 months; (e) vendors that improve to Yellow or above retain vendor relationship; vendors that remain Red after 6 months face procurement restrictions
Responsible (R): Sustainability Lead / Procurement
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 2 hours/vendor</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1176_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1176_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1176_Task11" name="Procurement integration">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Procurement integration: Integrate sustainability ratings into procurement decisions: (a) vendor scorecard per W44 includes sustainability dimension (weighted 15%); (b) Green-certified vendors: preferred status, longer contract terms, first consideration for new SKU allocation; (c) Yellow vendors: standard terms, improvement expected; (d) Orange vendors: no new SKU allocation until improvement; (e) Red vendors: progressive phase-out per procurement policy; (f) sustainability score included in bid evaluation per W632 competitive bidding
Responsible (R): Procurement / Category Manager
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: Ongoing</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1176_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1176_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1176_Task12" name="Annual reporting">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Annual reporting: Sustainability certification results feed ESG report per W694: (a) % of COGS from Green-certified vendors (target: 40% by Year 3), (b) % of vendors meeting minimum standards (target: 90%), (c) corrective action completion rate, (d) improvement trends
Responsible (R): Sustainability Lead
Accountable (A): ESG Manager
Duration: 4 hours/year</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1176_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1176_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1176_End13" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1176_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1176_Annotation14">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-317 (ensure controlled execution — Social Impact &amp; Governance (PA-25.2).) | - operational: Sustainability Lead review and approval gate
Owner: Sustainability Lead</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1176_Assoc15" sourceRef="W1176_Annotation14" targetRef="W1176_Start5" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1176_Flow16" sourceRef="W1176_Start5" targetRef="W1176_Task6" />
