    <bpmn:process id="W_W1331" name="W1331. Employee Volunteer Program Management, Tracking &amp; Impact Measurement" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Annual CSR calendar planning; quarterly volunteer event scheduling; or disaster relief activation requiring employee volunteer deployment
Frequency: ~4–6 organized volunteer events per year (company-wide); ~1–2 local events per store per year; ad-hoc disaster relief deployment
Volume: Target: 40% employee participation rate (2,700 of 6,911 employees volunteer at least once per year); ~8,000–10,000 volunteer hours/year
Owner: CSR Coordinator (within Marketing/HR)
Participants: CHRO, Store Manager (local event coordination), NGO Partner, Department Heads (team participation), Sustainability Lead (impact measurement)
Source: workflow W1331 — Employee Volunteer Program Management, Tracking &amp; Impact Measurement</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1331_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1331_Lane1" name="CSR Coordinator">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1331_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1331_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1331_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1331_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1331_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1331_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1331_Lane2" name="Sustainability Lead">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1331_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1331_End11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1331_Start4" name="Annual CSR calendar planning; quarterly volunteer event scheduling; or disaster relief…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1331_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1331_Task5" name="Annual volunteer program planning">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Annual volunteer program planning: CSR Coordinator develops annual volunteer calendar: (a) schedule 4–6 company-wide volunteer events aligned with national events (National Housing Month in October, Earth Day in April, National Volunteer Month in December, BuildRight Foundation anniversary), (b) allocate volunteer event budget: materials, transportation, meals, safety equipment, (c) identify NGO partners for each event (Habitat for Humanity Philippines, Philippine Red Cross, local LGU partnerships), (d) set participation targets by region, (e) obtain CEO and CHRO approval for calendar and budget
Responsible (R): CSR Coordinator
Accountable (A): CHRO / CEO
Duration: 3–5 days</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1331_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1331_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1331_Task6" name="Event logistics &amp; registration">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Event logistics &amp; registration: For each volunteer event: (a) CSR Coordinator publishes event details via internal communication (company app, email, bulletin board): date, location, activity description, capacity, skills required, safety requirements, (b) employee self-registration via HR portal or volunteer management app, (c) Store Manager approves volunteer time-off for participating employees (ensuring store operations coverage), (d) CSR Coordinator coordinates with NGO partner on activity scope, materials, and safety briefing, (e) arrange transportation for volunteers (company shuttle or travel allowance for provincial events)
Responsible (R): CSR Coordinator / Store Manager
Accountable (A): CHRO
Duration: 3–5 days per event</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1331_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1331_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1331_Task7" name="Event execution">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Event execution: (a) CSR Coordinator conducts safety briefing at event site: hazards, emergency procedures, PPE requirements (hard hats for construction events, gloves for cleanup events), (b) employee volunteers execute activity (house building, community cleanup, school renovation, disaster relief packing), (c) document event with photos and videos for internal communication and ESG reporting, (d) collect participant feedback via post-event survey (satisfaction, suggestions)
Responsible (R): CSR Coordinator / NGO Partner
Accountable (A): CHRO
Duration: Event day (4–8 hours)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1331_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1331_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1331_Task8" name="Attendance &amp; hours tracking">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Attendance &amp; hours tracking: (a) CSR Coordinator records attendance and volunteer hours per employee via HR portal: employee ID, event, hours contributed, (b) volunteer hours feed into individual employee records per W51 for training/development tracking, (c) volunteer hours feed into ESG data collection per W694: total volunteer hours, participation rate by gender, participation rate by region, (d) recognize top volunteers in quarterly company newsletter and annual awards per W72
Responsible (R): CSR Coordinator / HR
Accountable (A): CHRO
Duration: 1–2 hours per event</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1331_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1331_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1331_Task9" name="Impact measurement">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Impact measurement: Sustainability Lead measures social impact of volunteer events: (a) output metrics: houses built, classrooms renovated, families served, trees planted, relief packs assembled, (b) outcome metrics: community satisfaction survey, beneficiary feedback, (c) economic value: volunteer hours × average hourly wage (local wage-proxy methodology per PSA/ILO wage statistics), (d) compile impact data for quarterly ESG dashboard per W1321 and annual sustainability report per W694
Responsible (R): Sustainability Lead / CSR Coordinator
Accountable (A): VP Marketing
Duration: 2–3 days/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1331_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1331_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1331_Task10" name="Disaster relief volunteer deployment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Disaster relief volunteer deployment: When a natural disaster (typhoon, earthquake, flood) affects a BuildRight community: (a) CEO authorizes emergency volunteer deployment, (b) CSR Coordinator coordinates with Philippine Red Cross or DSWD for volunteer assignment, (c) Store Manager in affected area organizes local employee volunteers, (d) safety protocol: volunteers deployed only to areas declared safe by LGU, insurance coverage verified per W59, (e) rapid impact reporting: volunteer hours, relief distributed, community impact within 30 days
Responsible (R): CSR Coordinator / CEO
Accountable (A): CHRO
Duration: Per event</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1331_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1331_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1331_End11" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1331_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1331_Annotation12">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-317 (ensure controlled execution — Social Impact &amp; Governance (PA-25.2).) | - operational: regional event scheduling and local event options; operational: safety briefings, PPE provision, and insurance coverage confirmation per W59; operational: tracking both output and outcome indicators
Owner: CSR Coordinator (within Marketing/HR)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1331_Assoc13" sourceRef="W1331_Annotation12" targetRef="W1331_Start4" associationDirection="None" />
