    <bpmn:process id="W_W1332" name="W1332. Indigenous Peoples (IP) &amp; Cultural Sensitivity Compliance for Store Expansion" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: New store site selection per W223 in an area with identified Indigenous Peoples (IP) communities; or LGU consultation revealing IP presence; or NCIP (National Commission on Indigenous Peoples) notification
Frequency: Estimated 3–5 new store projects per year may intersect with IP areas (particularly in Mindanao, Cordillera, and Palawan)
Volume: 10–15 new stores per year; ~30% may require IP compliance assessment
Owner: VP Legal
Participants: COO, External Affairs Manager, NCIP Representative, IP Community Leader, Director, Facilities &amp; Real Estate, Sustainability Lead
Source: workflow W1332 — Indigenous Peoples (IP) &amp; Cultural Sensitivity Compliance for Store Expansion</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1332_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1332_Lane1" name="External Affairs Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1332_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1332_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1332_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1332_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1332_Lane2" name="VP Legal">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1332_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1332_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1332_Lane3" name="Store Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1332_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1332_End12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1332_Start5" name="New store site selection per W223 in an area with identified Indigenous Peoples (IP)…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1332_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1332_Task6" name="IP presence screening">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: IP presence screening: During site selection per W223: (a) External Affairs Manager checks NCIP Ancestral Domain Registry for the proposed site location, (b) checks LGU Comprehensive Land Use Plan for IP community designations, (c) consults with NCIP regional office on any pending or approved Certificates of Ancestral Domain Title (CADT) in the area, (d) if IP presence confirmed or likely: classify site as &quot;IP-sensitive&quot; and trigger FPIC process
Responsible (R): External Affairs Manager
Accountable (A): VP Legal
Duration: 3–5 days per site</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1332_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1332_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1332_Task7" name="FPIC process initiation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: FPIC process initiation: For IP-sensitive sites: (a) VP Legal coordinates with NCIP to initiate FPIC process, (b) submit project description to NCIP: store location, size, expected employment, economic impact, environmental impact, (c) NCIP determines FPIC requirement level based on impact assessment, (d) NCIP assigns a focal person and facilitates community consultation process
Responsible (R): VP Legal / External Affairs Manager
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: 1–2 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1332_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1332_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1332_Task8" name="Community consultation &amp; engagement">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Community consultation &amp; engagement: External Affairs Manager conducts community engagement: (a) attend community assembly (organized by NCIP) to present BuildRight&#x27;s project to IP community leaders and members, (b) present: store concept, employment opportunities for community members, potential impact (noise, traffic, water, land use), community benefit proposals (scholarship program, infrastructure improvement, skills training per W52), (c) respond to community questions and concerns transparently, (d) document all community interactions with NCIP observer present
Responsible (R): External Affairs Manager / VP Legal
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: 2–4 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1332_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1332_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1332_Task9" name="Community Benefit Agreement (CBA) negotiation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Community Benefit Agreement (CBA) negotiation: If community supports the project: (a) negotiate CBA with IP community leaders (facilitated by NCIP): employment quota for community members, community development fund (percentage of store revenue or fixed annual amount), environmental protection commitments, cultural heritage preservation (avoiding disruption to sacred sites, traditional livelihoods), local procurement commitment (sourcing from community enterprises per W115), (b) CBA reviewed by VP Legal for legal compliance and risk assessment, (c) CBA signed by BuildRight representative, IP community leaders, and NCIP
Responsible (R): External Affairs Manager / VP Legal
Accountable (A): CEO
Duration: 2–4 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1332_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1332_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1332_Task10" name="FPIC certification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: FPIC certification: NCIP issues Certificate of Compliance with FPIC after: (a) community assembly with required quorum, (b) documented consent resolution from IP community, (c) signed CBA, (d) VP Legal retains FPIC certificate and CBA for regulatory compliance file per W506
Responsible (R): VP Legal / NCIP
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: 2–4 weeks after Step 4</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1332_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1332_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1332_Task11" name="Ongoing compliance &amp; relationship management">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Ongoing compliance &amp; relationship management: After store opening: (a) Store Manager maintains relationship with IP community: regular communication, CBA compliance monitoring, community liaison visits, (b) Sustainability Lead monitors CBA compliance: employment of community members, community development fund disbursement, environmental commitments, (c) annual CBA compliance report prepared for NCIP and ESG reporting per W694, (d) if community grievances arise: External Affairs Manager mediates per grievance mechanism in CBA
Responsible (R): Store Manager / Sustainability Lead / External Affairs Manager
Accountable (A): VP Legal
Duration: Ongoing</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1332_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1332_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1332_End12" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1332_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1332_Annotation13">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-317 (ensure controlled execution — Social Impact &amp; Governance (PA-25.2).) | - operational: VP Legal review and approval gate
Owner: VP Legal</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1332_Assoc14" sourceRef="W1332_Annotation13" targetRef="W1332_Start5" associationDirection="None" />
