    <bpmn:process id="W_W1333" name="W1333. Stakeholder Engagement Matrix &amp; Materiality Assessment Refresh" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Annual ESG reporting cycle (Q1); or significant change in stakeholder landscape (new regulator, new community, IPO preparation, major incident); or every 2 years as best practice
Frequency: Full materiality assessment every 2 years; annual stakeholder engagement matrix update; continuous stakeholder feedback collection
Volume: ~10–15 stakeholder groups; ~30–40 ESG topics assessed for materiality
Owner: Sustainability Lead
Participants: CEO, VP Legal, CFO, COO, CHRO, VP Marketing, External Sustainability Advisor, stakeholder representatives
Source: workflow W1333 — Stakeholder Engagement Matrix &amp; Materiality Assessment Refresh</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1333_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1333_Lane1" name="Sustainability Lead">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1333_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1333_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1333_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1333_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1333_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1333_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1333_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1333_End10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1333_Start3" name="Annual ESG reporting cycle (Q1); or significant change in stakeholder landscape (new…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1333_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1333_Task4" name="Stakeholder identification &amp; mapping">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Stakeholder identification &amp; mapping: Sustainability Lead updates stakeholder engagement matrix: (a) identify all stakeholder groups: (i) shareholders/owners, (ii) employees (6,911), (iii) customers (B2C, B2B, trade), (iv) vendors/suppliers (~800–1,000), (v) government/regulators (BIR, DENR, DOLE, SEC, LGU), (vi) communities (200 store locations), (vii) lenders/banks, (viii) insurance partners, (ix) industry associations, (x) media, (xi) NGOs/civil society, (xii) academic institutions; (b) classify stakeholders by: influence (ability to affect BuildRight&#x27;s operations), impact (degree to which BuildRight affects them), proximity (direct vs. indirect relationship); (c) map stakeholders on a 2×2 matrix: high influence/high impact (priority engagement), high influence/low impact (keep satisfied), low influence/high impact (keep informed), low influence/low impact (monitor)
Responsible (R): Sustainability Lead
Accountable (A): VP Legal
Duration: 2–3 days</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1333_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1333_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1333_Task5" name="ESG topic universe compilation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: ESG topic universe compilation: Sustainability Lead compiles comprehensive ESG topic list: (a) environmental: GHG emissions, energy management, water stewardship, waste management, circular economy, biodiversity, packaging sustainability, hazardous materials; (b) social: employee health &amp; safety, labor practices, diversity &amp; inclusion, training &amp; development, community impact, customer safety, supply chain labor standards, data privacy; (c) governance: anti-corruption, risk management, board governance, tax transparency, business ethics, cyber security, AI ethics, regulatory compliance; (d) cross-cutting: climate resilience, disaster preparedness, human rights, economic contribution; (e) reference GRI Standards topics, SASB Retail standards, and Philippine-specific issues (IP rights, disaster resilience, informal worker welfare)
Responsible (R): Sustainability Lead / External Advisor
Accountable (A): VP Legal
Duration: 3–5 days</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1333_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1333_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1333_Task6" name="Stakeholder engagement &amp; feedback collection">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Stakeholder engagement &amp; feedback collection: Sustainability Lead collects stakeholder perspectives on ESG topics: (a) Employee survey: online survey distributed to all employees — rate importance of 30–40 ESG topics on 1–5 scale, (b) Customer survey: embedded in CSAT survey per W65 — 5–10 ESG questions, (c) Vendor survey: distributed via vendor portal per W705 — ESG topics relevant to supply chain, (d) Executive interviews: 30–45 min interviews with each VP — assess business impact of each ESG topic, (e) External expert consultation: interview External Sustainability Advisor on emerging ESG trends in Philippine retail, (f) Community feedback: aggregate community complaints and feedback per W209 from past 12 months
Responsible (R): Sustainability Lead / External Advisor
Accountable (A): CEO
Duration: 3–4 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1333_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1333_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1333_Task7" name="Materiality matrix construction">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Materiality matrix construction: Sustainability Lead constructs materiality matrix: (a) X-axis: importance to stakeholders (average survey score + qualitative input weighting), (b) Y-axis: impact on BuildRight&#x27;s business (executive interview scores + financial impact assessment), (c) plot all ESG topics on matrix; topics in upper-right quadrant = most material, (d) classify topics: Most Material (top-right quadrant — priority for strategy and reporting), Material (mid-range — report and monitor), Less Material (lower-left — acknowledge and monitor), (e) validate matrix with Executive Team for business plausibility
Responsible (R): Sustainability Lead / External Advisor
Accountable (A): CEO
Duration: 3–5 days</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1333_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1333_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1333_Task8" name="ESG strategy alignment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: ESG strategy alignment: Sustainability Lead maps materiality results to BuildRight&#x27;s ESG strategy and targets per W1321: (a) confirm that current ESG targets cover all Most Material topics; if gaps exist, propose new targets, (b) confirm that W694 annual report addresses all Most Material topics, (c) identify emerging topics (previously not material but rising in importance) — develop monitoring plan, (d) identify declining topics (previously material but now less so) — consider reducing reporting emphasis, (e) present materiality assessment results to Board ESG Committee for approval
Responsible (R): Sustainability Lead
Accountable (A): Board ESG Committee
Duration: 2–3 days</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1333_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1333_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1333_Task9" name="Communication &amp; integration">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Communication &amp; integration: Sustainability Lead communicates materiality results: (a) share with Department Heads: relevant material topics and their responsibilities, (b) update ESG reporting template per W694 to reflect refreshed materiality, (c) update stakeholder engagement plan for next 2 years based on feedback, (d) publish summary materiality matrix in annual sustainability report per W694, (e) integrate into enterprise risk register per W122 — Most Material ESG topics should be reflected as risks with appropriate KRI monitoring per W1329
Responsible (R): Sustainability Lead
Accountable (A): VP Legal
Duration: 2–3 days</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1333_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1333_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1333_End10" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1333_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1333_Annotation11">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-317 (ensure controlled execution — Social Impact &amp; Governance (PA-25.2).) | - operational: Store Manager promotion and dedicated survey time during team huddles; operational: using multiple engagement channels (survey, in-store, social media, focus groups); operational: conducting interviews during annual planning cycle
Owner: Sustainability Lead</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1333_Assoc12" sourceRef="W1333_Annotation11" targetRef="W1333_Start3" associationDirection="None" />
