    <bpmn:process id="W_W1479" name="W1479. Disaster Relief &amp; Community Resilience Program Coordination &amp; Emergency Product Distribution" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Natural disaster event (typhoon, earthquake, flooding) affecting BuildRight store communities; or LGU request for emergency building material supply; or DSWD/Red Cross coordination request
Frequency: ~3–5 major disaster events/year in the Philippines (typhoons); localized flooding events ~10–15/year
Volume: Per major event: ~50–100 affected stores; emergency product distribution of PHP 5–20M in building materials, tarps, water tanks, tools
Owner: COO
Participants: CEO, COO, VP Merchandising, DC Manager, Store Manager, Sustainability Lead, VP Legal, LGU officials, DSWD, Red Cross, Community Leaders
Source: workflow W1479 — Disaster Relief &amp; Community Resilience Program Coordination &amp; Emergency Product Distribution</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1479_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1479_Lane1" name="COO">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1479_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1479_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1479_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1479_Lane2" name="VP Merchandising">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1479_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1479_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1479_Lane3" name="Sustainability Lead">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1479_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1479_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1479_End12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1479_Start5" name="Natural disaster event (typhoon, earthquake, flooding) affecting BuildRight store…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1479_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1479_Task6" name="Disaster event activation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Disaster event activation: (a) when a typhoon (signal 3+), earthquake (magnitude 5+), or major flooding event is forecast/confirmed: COO activates BuildRight&#x27;s Disaster Response Protocol; (b) COO assesses: (i) which BuildRight stores and DCs are in the affected path? (ii) pre-position high-demand items at at-risk stores: tarps, plywood, nails, cement, water containers, generators, batteries, flashlights; (iii) coordinate with DC Managers to pre-stage emergency inventory; (c) CEO approves emergency product allocation budget (initial PHP 5M authorization, up to PHP 20M for major events)
Responsible (R): COO / CEO
Accountable (A): CEO
Duration: 2–4 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1479_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1479_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1479_Task7" name="Emergency product allocation &amp; distribution">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Emergency product allocation &amp; distribution: (a) VP Merchandising allocates emergency inventory from DCs to affected stores: (i) priority items: tarps (for roof coverage), plywood/nails (for emergency boarding), water containers, portable generators, flashlights, batteries, safety boots, gloves; (ii) bypass standard replenishment process — emergency transfer orders per W22 with &quot;Disaster Relief&quot; priority; (b) Store Manager at affected stores: (i) pre-disaster: stage emergency items at store entrance for rapid customer access, (ii) during disaster: store closed for safety — secure inventory per W1389, (iii) post-disaster: reopen ASAP with extended hours to serve community rebuilding needs
Responsible (R): VP Merchandising / DC Manager / Store Manager
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: Per W22 emergency</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1479_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1479_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1479_Task8" name="Community donation &amp; LGU coordination">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Community donation &amp; LGU coordination: (a) COO coordinates with LGU disaster management offices (MDRRMO — Municipal/City Disaster Risk Reduction and Management Office) in affected areas: (i) offer BuildRight as emergency building material supplier, (ii) donate materials for community shelters and repair of public facilities (schools, health centers), (iii) provide logistics support (BuildRight trucks for relief goods distribution); (b) Sustainability Lead manages donation documentation: (i) itemized list of donated materials with value, (ii) LGU acknowledgment receipts, (iii) photographs for ESG reporting per W1330; (c) VP Legal ensures donations comply with tax deductibility requirements per BIR regulations
Responsible (R): COO / Sustainability Lead / VP Legal
Accountable (A): CEO
Duration: Per event</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1479_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1479_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1479_Task9" name="Volunteer deployment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Volunteer deployment: (a) Sustainability Lead activates employee volunteer program per W1331: (i) employees in unaffected stores volunteer for deployment to affected stores (1–3 day assignments), (ii) volunteers assist with: store cleanup, emergency product distribution, community cleanup drives, temporary shelter assembly; (b) HR ensures volunteers are covered by workers&#x27; compensation during volunteer deployment per DOLE requirements; (c) Store Manager manages volunteer assignments and logistics (transportation, meals)
Responsible (R): Sustainability Lead / HR / Store Manager
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: Per event</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1479_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1479_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1479_Task10" name="Post-disaster rebuilding support">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Post-disaster rebuilding support: (a) in the 1–3 months following a major disaster: VP Merchandising adjusts assortment in affected stores: (i) increase stock levels of rebuilding materials (cement, rebar, roofing, plywood, nails, paint), (ii) coordinate with vendors for expedited delivery to affected region, (iii) offer &quot;Rebuild&quot; bundle pricing per W14 — discounted material packages for home repair; (b) Category Manager deploys project estimation teams per W1090 to assist homeowners with material quantity calculation for rebuilding; (c) Trade Account team prioritizes credit applications from contractors working on reconstruction per W1269 — fast-track approval for rebuilding contractors
Responsible (R): VP Merchandising / Category Manager
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: 1–3 months post-disaster</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1479_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1479_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1479_Task11" name="ESG reporting &amp; lessons learned">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: ESG reporting &amp; lessons learned: (a) Sustainability Lead compiles disaster response report for ESG disclosure per W1330: (i) total donations (PHP value, items), (ii) employee volunteer hours, (iii) community impact stories; (b) COO conducts post-event review: (i) was pre-positioning effective? (ii) were emergency transfers timely? (iii) were LGU partnerships effective? (iv) what product categories ran out first? — update disaster inventory planning; (c) annual: update Disaster Response Protocol based on lessons learned
Responsible (R): Sustainability Lead / COO
Accountable (A): CEO
Duration: 1–2 days post-event</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1479_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1479_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1479_End12" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1479_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1479_Annotation13">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-317 (ensure controlled execution — Social Impact &amp; Governance (PA-25.2).) | - operational: coordinating only with LGU-declared safe zones
Owner: COO</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1479_Assoc14" sourceRef="W1479_Annotation13" targetRef="W1479_Start5" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1479_Flow15" sourceRef="W1479_Start5" targetRef="W1479_Task6" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1479_Flow16" sourceRef="W1479_Task6" targetRef="W1479_Task7" />
