    <bpmn:process id="W_W1480" name="W1480. Supplier Diversity Program, Small &amp; Medium Enterprise (SME) Vendor Development &amp; Capacity Building" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Annual procurement strategy review; or government mandate for SME inclusion in supply chain; or ESG social impact target setting
Frequency: Annual program planning; quarterly vendor development workshops; monthly SME vendor performance review
Volume: Target: ≥ 20% of vendor base as MSMEs within 3 years (per W115); currently ~150–200 SME vendors (~20% of the ~800–1,000 base, per the Background)
Owner: VP Merchandising
Participants: Category Manager, Buyer, Procurement, Sustainability Lead, Finance (payment terms), SME Vendor, DTI (MSME development programs)
Source: workflow W1480 — Supplier Diversity Program, Small &amp; Medium Enterprise (SME) Vendor Development &amp; Capacity Building</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1480_LaneSet5">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1480_Lane1" name="Category Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1480_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1480_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1480_Start6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1480_Lane2" name="Procurement">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1480_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1480_Lane3" name="VP Merchandising">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1480_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1480_Lane4" name="Sustainability Lead">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1480_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1480_End12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1480_Start6" name="Annual procurement strategy review; or government mandate for SME inclusion in supply…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1480_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1480_Task7" name="SME vendor identification &amp; assessment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: SME vendor identification &amp; assessment: (a) Category Manager identifies product categories suitable for SME sourcing: (i) categories where local products offer unique value (regional tiles, handcrafted fixtures, indigenous materials), (ii) categories where SME sourcing reduces import dependency, (iii) categories where local SMEs exist but are not yet BuildRight vendors; (b) Procurement conducts SME capability assessment: (i) product quality sampling and testing, (ii) production capacity (units/month vs. BuildRight demand), (iii) business registration (DTI/SEC), (iv) tax compliance (BIR registration), (v) GS1 barcode capability per W1345, (vi) logistics capability (direct-to-store or DC delivery)
Responsible (R): Category Manager / Procurement
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 2 hours/vendor</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1480_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1480_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1480_Task8" name="SME vendor onboarding &amp; development">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: SME vendor onboarding &amp; development: (a) for SMEs that pass initial assessment but have capability gaps: Procurement creates a Vendor Development Plan: (i) Quality: establish product specifications and quality testing protocol per W36; provide feedback on sample rejections with specific improvement guidance; (ii) Packaging &amp; Barcoding: assist SME with GS1 Philippines registration and barcode printing — connect with GS1 Philippines MSME assistance program; (iii) Volume scaling: start with regional deployment (10–20 stores) before nationwide rollout; provide demand forecast visibility so SME can plan production; (iv) Financial: offer shorter payment terms initially (Net 15 instead of Net 30) while SME builds cash flow capacity; connect SME with DTI&#x27;s Pondo sa Pagbabago at Pag-asenso (P3) microfinance program; (v) Logistics: allow SME to deliver to regional DC only (not to all stores) — BuildRight handles DC-to-store distribution per W4
Responsible (R): Procurement / Category Manager
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: Per vendor (ongoing)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1480_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1480_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1480_Task9" name="Quarterly SME vendor development workshops">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Quarterly SME vendor development workshops: (a) VP Merchandising hosts quarterly vendor development workshop for SME suppliers (rotating locations — Davao, Cebu, Manila): (i) session 1: BuildRight quality standards and product specification requirements, (ii) session 2: packaging, labeling, and GS1 barcode compliance per W1345, (iii) session 3: supply chain management — demand forecasting, order fulfillment, and delivery scheduling, (iv) session 4: financial management — working capital, payment terms, and VAT invoicing; (b) invite DTI MSME development office to co-facilitate; (c) provide networking opportunity for SMEs to learn from each other and from larger BuildRight vendors
Responsible (R): VP Merchandising / Procurement
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 1 day/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1480_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1480_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1480_Task10" name="SME vendor performance monitoring">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: SME vendor performance monitoring: (a) monthly: Category Manager reviews SME vendor performance metrics: (i) on-time delivery rate, (ii) quality rejection rate, (iii) fill rate (% of ordered quantity delivered), (iv) barcode compliance rate per W1345; (b) for underperforming SMEs: (i) Category Manager provides specific feedback and improvement timeline, (ii) if performance does not improve within 3 months: transition product to alternative vendor while maintaining development support for the SME; (c) for high-performing SMEs: (i) increase order volume and expand to more stores, (ii) consider for private-label development per W1, (iii) feature in BuildRight&#x27;s &quot;Proudly Filipino&quot; marketing campaign per W14
Responsible (R): Category Manager
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 2 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1480_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1480_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1480_Task11" name="ESG reporting &amp; program evaluation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: ESG reporting &amp; program evaluation: (a) Sustainability Lead tracks Supplier Diversity Program metrics for ESG disclosure per W1330: (i) number of SME vendors, (ii) % of total procurement spend allocated to SMEs, (iii) SME vendor growth (revenue increase year-over-year), (iv) jobs created/supported in SME supply chain; (b) annually: VP Merchandising evaluates program ROI: (i) SME vendor product margin vs. import alternatives, (ii) supply chain reliability (SME vs. international vendors), (iii) customer reception of SME-sourced products, (iv) ESG reporting value; (c) adjust program targets for next year based on evaluation
Responsible (R): Sustainability Lead / VP Merchandising
Accountable (A): CEO
Duration: 2 days/year</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1480_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1480_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1480_End12" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1480_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1480_Annotation13">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-317 (ensure controlled execution — Social Impact &amp; Governance (PA-25.2).) | - operational: capability levels
Owner: VP Merchandising</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
